  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of the 18th-Century Sugar Mill at Bras d&apos;Eau National Park</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Established as a working plantation in 1786 and today a national park, Bras d&apos;Eau endures as a reminder of the impacts of human slavery and indentured servitude on the island of Mauritiuss agricultural and industrial development and environmental transformation between the 18th and early 20th centuries. This project involves the documentation and development of a conservation plan for the plantations historic sugar mill.</narrative>
  </description>
